WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday. Greetings from beautiful and somewhat windy, Chamberland, South Dakota. So, Hank, earlier today

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.399
I signed what I believed to be every copy of Turtles All The Way Down

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.210
currently available for sale or borrowing in Sioux Falls, South Dakota,

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:16.829
and I met a lot of wonderful librarians, and booksellers, and confused Target shoppers.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.319
And I also filmed the whole thing, and it would have made a great video,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.580
but then I destroyed my memory card. What happened--and I desperately wish I were making this up--

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.619
is that I was eating pretzel chips by the handful, because of course I was, while fiddling with my memory card and--um--

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.019
somehow my hands got confused about what was what.

00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:36.509
I mean, to be fair, a memory card and a pretzel chip have almost the exact same thickness and overall weight,

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:41.100
but really that's not a great excuse. So yeah, what happened is that I put the memory card into my mouth,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.329
and then I chewed it. The weird part--well actually I guess it's all weird parts--but the weirdest part

00:00:45.329 --> 00:00:49.468
is that when I bit down on the memory card, my first thought was, 'huh that pretzel

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:53.999
chip is very crunchy,' and so my natural reaction was to attempt to chew it again. Now,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.799
it does not appear to be damaged--there's a couple very small tooth marks--but, it's toast.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.009
I'm gonna let this frustration go in a minute, but just as a parting remark,

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:05.970
I would like to note that it says right here on the memory card that it is an 'Extreme Pro

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:11.939
Memory Card'. And, look, obviously I shouldn't have chewed on my memory card, but I would argue that any non-food

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:17.699
Item that can be destroyed by human chewing should not describe itself as 'Extreme Pro'. Alright,

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.670
let's go on a tour bus bus tour. Hey, that's a palindrome--nope--

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:24.029
no, it is definitely not. So, the first thing you see when you come inside

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:30.389
is the driver's seat--that's where Brock lives. Once you walk onto the bus, you come to the first seating area

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:35.189
which I like to think of as the office. It's sort of the quiet part of the bus where everybody's always on their computer answering

00:01:35.189 --> 00:01:35.979
emails, etc.

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:41.099
But the great thing about the office, is that it's also sort of the dining room due to its proximity to the kitchen. By the

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.780
way, there are the offending pretzel chips...

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:48.000
We really have everything you need in a kitchen; a microwave, a sink, and a banana holder. Past that, you get to the

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:54.929
bathroom. We have a very nicely appointed, if somewhat small, bathroom; but there's one very important rule about the bus bathroom

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:59.669
which is no pooping in the bus bathroom, not because of like moral concerns,

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:06.149
but the tubes are too small. Then you come to our refrigerator, which is mostly diet soda, La Croix,

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:10.649
there's some beer, there's some baby carrots down there that nobody's ever eaten... And then past the bathroom,

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:15.410
we have the bedrooms: eight beautiful bunks. Here's mine. I'm sorry

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:20.179
I didn't make my bed for you, but here are two cute puppies I got at Target Headquarters. Hank's bunk is directly beneath mine--

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:24.260
--he didn't make his bed either. And then past the bedroom, is the second seating area

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.490
which I like to think of as, like, the rec room because it contains my Nintendo switch.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:31.429
So, this is kind of the hangout area--because the engines right back there,

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:35.480
it's a little bit louder and there's more side-to-side motion; and when we first started on tour,

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.119
everyone was really nauseated and nobody wanted to sit back here,

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:43.370
but now we've all got our bus legs. Now, the great thing about the bus is that there's so much storage, like you know, that bag

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:49.100
which contains 850 plastic Turtles. In fact, there's plastic Turtles everywhere. We've got plastic Turtles in the shoe closet,

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:53.540
we've got a cute little turtle moose in the Sharpie drawer--yes, we have a Sharpie drawer,--

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:58.040
--we've even got some Holden turtle fields in the microwave.See, he's wearing his people hunting hat.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:01.579
We've even got Turtles with top hats in our popcorn and applesauce drawer.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.609
It really is kind of a Turtles all the way down situation. Okay, Hank,

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.880
I'm gonna go hide some signed plastic turtles here in Chamberlain, South Dakota.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:11.509
We're leaving them everywhere we stopped; you can find hints to their location on my Instagram story.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:14.510
And thanks again to everyone in Sioux Falls who was so incredibly nice to me--

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.980
--sorry that I chewed on all of our memories. Hank, I will see you on Friday--actually

00:03:19.019 --> 00:03:21.649
I'll see you like on Thursday, but you know what I mean.

